      "id": "alloy_system_1",
      "name": "refractory high-entropy alloy",
      "material_category": "refractory high-entropy alloy",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 1,
          "section": "Abstract",
          "quote": "At present, refractory high-entropy alloys (RHEAs) containing high-melting refractory metal elements have excellent room temperature and high-temperature properties, and their potential high-temperature application value has attracted widespread attention in the high-temperature field.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "35b8307d2cdbf687:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": 22,
          "section": null,
          "quote": "Among the studies on non-metallic elements added to realize the enhancement of the second phase of non-coherent precipitation, there are many studies on RHEAs with C and Si elements added and studies on N and O yet [143, 178].",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "35b8307d2cdbf687:part:002"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "alloy_system_2",
      "name": "high-entropy boride ceramic",
      "material_category": "high-entropy ceramic",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 23,
          "section": null,
          "quote": "synthesized corresponding boride powders by carbothermal reduction of boron at 1600 °C using oxides, boron carbide, and carbon powders as raw materials and successfully prepared (Hf0.2Zr0.2Ta0.2Nb0.2Ti0.2)B2, (Hf0.2Zr0.2Mo0.2Nb0.2Ti0.2)B2, and (Hf0.2Mo0.2Ta0.2Nb0.2Ti0.2)B2 high-entropy ceramics by SPS at 2000 °C.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "35b8307d2cdbf687:part:002"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
